.TH CFFLATEXPAND 1 "2026-11-09" "import-citation-cff 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cfflatexpand \- expand CFF metadata in a LaTeX manuscript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfflatexpand
[\fIoption\fR]... \fImanuscript.tex\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfflatexpand
rewrites a LaTeX manuscript that uses the
.B import-citation-cff
package so that it can be built without the package and without its
Citation File Format (CFF) file, for example for a journal that accepts
only plain LaTeX files.
.PP
The metadata commands of the package, such as
.BR \ecff ,
are replaced with their values, and the loading of the package and
.B \eincludecff
are removed.
.B \ecffsetauthors
becomes the author declarations that it makes with the built-in author
styles, author style plugins, and custom templates; the
.B style
option of the package is its default style.
The declarations are rendered by
.BR lualatex ,
run with shell escape disabled.
The output still needs the class or package that provides them, such as
authblk.
.PP
Commands that import-citation-cff does not define are copied unchanged,
and metadata commands in verbatim text are not expanded.
.B \einput
and
.B \einclude
are also copied unchanged: to expand the metadata of included files,
first flatten the manuscript with
.BR latexpand (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-output=\fIfile\fR
Write to
.I file
instead of standard output;
.B \-
also means standard output.
The input file is never overwritten, and a failed conversion leaves an
existing
.I file
unchanged.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version, which is that of import-citation-cff, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing, so that the next argument is the manuscript even if
it starts with
.BR \- .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B cfflatexpand
exits with 0 on success and with 1 on an error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors go to standard error, with the location in the manuscript:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cfflatexpand: manuscript.tex:3:1: call \eincludecff before \ecff
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unsupported or invalid input produces no TeX output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Write the expanded manuscript to
.IR submission.tex :
.PP
.RS
.nf
cfflatexpand manuscript.tex \-o submission.tex
.fi
.RE
.PP
Expand a manuscript whose metadata commands are also in included files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
latexpand manuscript.tex > manuscript\-flat.tex
cfflatexpand manuscript\-flat.tex \-o submission.tex
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR latexpand (1),
.BR luatex (1)
.PP
The manual of import-citation-cff, shown by
.BR "texdoc import-citation-cff" .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/JSS95/cfflatex/issues.
